---
// The motivation section: why the platform exists, told in three beats.
// Static copy, no props; the wording is owner-approved verbatim.
---

<section class="section why-relab" aria-labelledby="why-relab-heading">
  <h2 id="why-relab-heading">Why Relab exists</h2>
  <div class="why-beats">
    <div class="why-beat">
      <h3 class="why-beat-label">Closed, and too slow</h3>
      <p>
        Circular-economy research depends on detailed product data: what things are made of, how
        they come apart, which parts matter. That data is scarce, mostly closed, and slow to
        produce. Producers hold it as proprietary, and small expert teams sampling by hand cannot
        keep pace with what reaches the market.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="why-beat">
      <h3 class="why-beat-label">Downstream, at the point of failure</h3>
      <p>
        So Relab goes downstream, to the people who already open products: repairers, refurbishers,
        dismantlers, recyclers. They meet products at the point of failure, a vantage that
        captures as-failed composition, wear, and recoverability that as-designed specifications
        never show.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="why-beat">
      <h3 class="why-beat-label">Value in both directions</h3>
      <p>
        The exchange runs both ways. Those observations feed back into the data infrastructure
        research and design rely on, and contributors get value back: composition insight,
        sustainability metrics, and guidance on the most circular R-strategy for what they are
        holding.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .why-relab h2 {
    margin: 0 0 1.4rem;
  }

  .why-beats {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 2rem;
  }

  /* Hairline top rule per beat: a flat drafting divider, no shadow. */
  .why-beat {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-page-border);
    padding-top: 0.9rem;
  }

  /* Sentence case, not the uppercase-with-tracking label treatment: these are
     phrases now rather than one-word tags, and caps would set them wrapping. */
  .why-beat-label {
    margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
    font-family: var(--relab-brand-font-mono), monospace;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.35;
    color: var(--color-on-surface);
  }

  .why-beat p {
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 60ch;
    font-size: var(--font-size-body-compact);
    line-height: var(--line-height-body-compact);
  }

  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .why-beats {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 1.4rem;
    }
  }
</style>
